&lt;&lt;~ set hud="aim" mode="draft" stance="🏛️🗡️" aperture="16/arc" ooda-ha="9/declare-glyphs" drift-ward="wave-one leans may outrun what the signed act and face-join code actually bind">>

Lares (Tasked Spirit) / Ink-Clerk:

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/observe-read-set-and-measurements`>>

!! ✶ Observe — read set and measurements

I read the boot carrier first, then the common brief, both wave-one notes, the I1 carrier and code at the checkout head. Repo access stayed read-only; I wrote only this handback. No suite ran. The boot names Ink-Clerk as Lorekeeper: cite grounds, mark uncertainty.

''MEASURED.'' No <code>&#64;intents-</code> implementation surfaced. The I1 carrier puts a fifth face plane beside <code>&#64;persona</code>, <code>&#64;circles</code>, <code>&#64;identities</code>, <code>&#64;sessions</code>; entries append and device atoms sign (carrier lines 47–55). Daemon summons dispatch locally (`verb-dispatcher.ts:1–20`; `operator-daemon-behavior.ts:601–650`). `runFaceJoin` first checks membership; an already seated joinee avoids add unless `summons.force === true`; forced or genuinely new join calls `addGroupMember` and re-seals (&#96;face-join.ts:220–255). Thus ordinary repeated grant can no-op, while force/re-founded-group paths can re-key. Concurrent partitions can both pass. No operation-id dedupe or pinned-hearth check guards Keyhive.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/decide-f1f6-rulings`>>

!! ◇ Decide — F1–F6 rulings

''F1 — DERIVED.'' Reuse the existing signed-act image with a new domain. `signed-act.ts:6–9,43–49,80–87` measures canonical JSON bytes, SHA-256 CID, domain in signed body, signature re-derivation and authorization; `persona-act.ts:20–26,62–71` supplies the domain-specific body/fold. House law: //one name, one relation// and //isomorphic by intent//. The carrier’s “content hash of issuer, verb, arguments and nonce” (line 50) defines intent identity fields but leaves their hash serialization/version distinct from the signed entry CID; use the shared canonical encoder and SHA-256 unless a compatibility version arises during schema design. No operator survivor here.

''F2 — CANON.'' Carrier line 66: “pin executor or require human answer naming atom”. Line 52 binds each `answer` to its `asks` id (“citing the ask’s id”); executor atom remains required where single-effect applies. No operator survivor.

''F3 — OPERATOR (one narrow choice).'' Measured above: outcome stand-down only helps readers that saw the outcome; Keyhive’s current membership check does not serialize partitions, and `force` bypasses it. Carrier line 66 pins a single-effect fleet-wide executor; carrier line 67 explicitly keeps losing acts visible after they happen. House law //safety lives in the effect// therefore requires the effect door to fence. The face-join summons must carry a stable operation ID and one pinned hearth/atom; Keyhive admission must atomically recognize that operation and refuse a competing hearth (same operation returns its recorded grant). The “single-effect verbs pin an executor” canon covers audience/pinning, but does not specify effect-door idempotency or whether the current face-join summons qualifies as such a verb. ''Lean:'' make it single-effect and pin one hearth; operation ID dedupes retries, while other hearths refuse. This closes F3’s residual.

''F4 — OPERATOR.'' Carrier lines 77, 79: voids name “the face’s roster passing a named edge”; an `every` intent reaches later joiners “unless its bound names a roster edge.” This binds membership to the signed fleet edge frontier (K17), not an intent-local clock or rival board; the carrier says “evaluate[] the audience against the roster it holds.” House law //consume K17’s frontier// and Wave C’s signed projection style derive the reader, but neither selects which frontier head an intent’s bound names nor how a finite campaign pins it. ''Lean:'' bound by explicit K17 frontier certificate/head at issue; no bound means later joins count, as carrier specifies. Avoid K17-R files.

''F5 — OPERATOR.'' Carrier line 54 gives “an issuer’s or the operator’s later word.” Wave C gives each face FCK, atom, sealed anchor, root/KEL authority (`k15-wave-c-lane.mem:47–51`). That settles face-scoped cryptographic authority, not which human/device relation represents “operator” for superseding a face act. ''Lean:'' root-authorized face operator act, with explicit delegation if a seat may act; any device atom alone should not suffice.

''F6 — CANON.'' Carrier lines 67, 77 and the reds 139–141 preserve duplicate outcomes, act-before-void receipts, and require unknown/duplicate witnesses before trusting zero. House law //show conflicts, never hide// plus //silent-zero// settles a read-only pane: display duplicates, void-after-act, and unknown frontier distinctly; count no winner when proof stays unknown. No operator survivor.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/act-final-kit-red-first`>>

!! ▶ Act — final kit, red-first

One I1 lane, in carrier order (line 149), staging interfaces only after each red/control/known positive:

# ''Plane + signed image.'' Hold face-plane derivation/registration, signed schema and node/browser openers. Red: unsigned plane URL / wrong domain; control: signed registered plane; positive: valid signed <code>&#64;persona</code> plane registration.
# ''Stand-down + effect classes + read winner.'' Hold common fold and verb registry. Red: prior outcome ignored / duplicate hidden; control: slot already answered stands down; positive: two idempotent partitioned effects converge, both receipts remain visible.
# ''Claims, release, causal voids.'' Hold claim fold, authority checks, bound reader. Red: zombie claimant after takeover or asleep device after void; control: unbounded intent honored; positive: current fenced claim acts.
# ''Face-join summons + CLI face per invocation.'' Hold daemon migration, face-join adapter and CLI selector. Red: two hearths race; control: second pinned hearth refuses; positive: same face syncs one summons, other face sees none. F3 fence and F4 bound must settle before schema freezes.
# ''Read-only daemon view.'' Hold pane/projection. Red: view writes or pipes intent; control: no capability yields no view; positive: authorized pane renders receipts, conflicts and unknowns.
# ''Rubric witness.'' Hold entry counter and witness. Red: seeded duplicate reads zero / ordinary save emits; control: keystrokes and one local save stay zero; positive: cross-device move produces one intent and outcome. Carrier reds 130–141 set this order.
# ''Far-agent relay seat remains out'' pending its own research, per carrier.

Live seams: keep W14–W16’s floor pin/admit gate pins/card filing/nexus-contract and K17-R frontier/lease/realm boards untouched; I1 consumes K17 frontier proof. Keep W26 slice 5’s floor accept act per `(face, Nexus)` untouched; I1 may reference it. F1, F2 and F6 carry no operator list entries. ''Operator list: F3 effect-door ID + pinned hearth rule; F4 explicit bounded K17 head semantics; F5 definition/delegation of face operator authority.''

Gaia’s laptop/phone story uses the shared intent ID and read-side stand-down while the phone sleeps. Elyncia: two hearths share a summons; only pinned hearth grants. Another face shares no entry.

↺ ''Aftermath:'' measured code exposes F3’s real double-act path; F1’s envelope derives cleanly from house canon. Three rulings remain before model freeze.

